      "writtenOn": "2015-05-07T03:27:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My original design goal is to implement SPS API based on the following SPI Slave APIs.\n\nhttps://developer.mbed.org/users/mbed_official/code/mbed/docs/tip/classmbed_1_1SPISlave.html\n\nFor example:\n/* Compute number of bytes received in the SPS  FIFO\n *\n *  @returns\n *    0 if no data,\n *    n number of bytes received\n */\nint sps_receive(uint32_t inst);\n\n/*\n *  Peek top byte in the SPS RX FIFO\n *  Don’t remove it from SPS RX FIFO\n *  @returns\n *    the data in the receive buffer\n */\nstatic uint8_t sps_top(uint32_t inst);\n\n/*\n * Read (Pop) 1-byte from the SPS RX FIFO\n * @param data Pointer to 8-bit data\n * @return pop count: 1 or 0\n */\nstatic int sps_read(uint32_t inst, uint8_t *data);\n\n/*\n * Reply (Push) a byte to the SPS TX FIFO\n * Fill the transmission buffer (SPS TX FIFO) with the value (1-byte) to be written out \n * as slave on the next received message from the master.\n * @param data Pointer to 8-bit data\n * @return push count: 1 or 0\n */\nstatic int sps_reply(uint32_t inst, const uint8_t data);",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 63,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "1d7e257e120474e82bc19fa46e916a14a51e5853",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
